{#- The notes of a GitHub Release (cog.toml, [changelog]): the commits
    since the last release by type, each linked, and for a breaking
    change its BREAKING CHANGE footer, whose later lines are indented
    under it (Tera strings take no escapes, so the newline in replace is
    a real one). The release page itself has the version and the
    comparison with the previous release. -#}
{% for value in commits | group_by_type -%}
### {{ value.0 | upper_first }}

{% for commit in value.1 -%}
- {% if commit.breaking_change %}**BREAKING:** {% endif %}{% if commit.scope %}**{{ commit.scope }}:** {% endif %}{{ commit.summary }} ([{{ commit.id | truncate(length=7, end="") }}]({{ repository_url }}/commit/{{ commit.id }}))
{% for footer in commit.footers -%}
{% if footer.footer -%}
{% if footer.footer.token is starting_with("BREAKING") %}  - {{ footer.footer.content | replace(from="
", to="
    ") }}
{% endif -%}
{% endif -%}
{% endfor -%}
{% endfor %}
{% endfor -%}
